Why This Will Still Matter in 2028
Three bets I'm making with this roadmap:

Models get better, but the hard problems move up the stack. Evals, agent reliability, context engineering, and domain integration will be more valuable in 2028, not less. The people who win aren't the ones who train models — they're the ones who make AI systems actually work in messy real-world conditions.
"Vibe coding" AI apps is easy; engineering them is not. Anyone can wire up an API call in 2028. Knowing how to debug a failing agent, design an eval suite, manage token costs at scale, and ship something that doesn't hallucinate — that's the moat.
Fundamentals > frameworks. LangChain might die. LlamaIndex might die. The concepts (retrieval, grounding, tool use, evals) will not. This roadmap teaches concepts through whatever framework is current.


